WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:38.416
In the fifth chapter, Lord Krishna

2
00:00:38.416 --> 00:00:42.791
explained the path to liberation
 through selfless karma yoga.

3
00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:45.083
And in the final part of that same chapter,

4
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.875
he presented Ashtanga Yoga
 as another foundation

5
00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:51.541
to attain that same liberation.

6
00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:53.500
Ashtanga Yoga means

7
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.416
the method of yoga that has eight stages.

8
00:00:57.416 --> 00:00:59.875
Now in the sixth chapter, Lord Krishna

9
00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:01.333
will describe this process

10
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:04.333
of Ashtanga Yoga in detail.

11
00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:10.500
In this first verse

12
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.208
of the sixth chapter, Krishna says

13
00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:16.083
that the person who performs his duties 
without desiring the fruits of action

14
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:18.458
is both a sannyasi

15
00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:22.583
and a yogi.

16
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:25.541
Sannyasa or renunciation of fruits doesn't mean

17
00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:27.333
abandoning your work

18
00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:30.791
or abandoning yajna.

19
00:01:30.791 --> 00:01:32.875
Lord Krishna is explaining here

20
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:35.708
that sannyasa and renunciation don't mean

21
00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:36.875
you should abandon your duties

22
00:01:36.875 --> 00:01:39.958
and worldly responsibilities.

23
00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:41.625
Here, renunciation means

24
00:01:41.625 --> 00:01:44.083
renouncing the expectation of results

25
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:46.250
and fulfilling your responsibilities

26
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.916
with complete dedication.

27
00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:52.458
This verse mentions the word "karma-phalam,"

28
00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:55.541
which refers to the consequences 
of a person's actions.

29
00:01:55.541 --> 00:01:57.583
Often people desire

30
00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.083
wealth, respect,

31
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:02.375
and personal happiness through their actions.

32
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:06.250
But Krishna clarifies that a person who is truly

33
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.458
walking the spiritual path,

34
00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:10.583
doesn't act out of desire

35
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:12.250
for these results.

36
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.750
Such a person completes his 
work not for selfish gain,

37
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:15.750
but

38
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.250
with a spirit of service and duty.

39
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.333
he fulfills his work.

40
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:20.583
Lord Krishna says

41
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.750
such a person is both a sannyasi—

42
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.375
because he has renounced
 attachment to fruits of action—

43
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:31.416
and also a yogi—who through performing 
action selflessly and

44
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:34.083
is making spiritual progress.

45
00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:36.250
True sannyasa and renunciation

46
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.708
isn't abandoning action,

47
00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:39.166
but abandoning attachment

48
00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:40.916
to the results of action.

49
00:02:40.916 --> 00:02:42.083
A true yogi

50
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:44.166
fulfills all his duties

51
00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:47.083
and keeps his mind and attention

52
00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.625
centered not on personal

53
00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:52.291
gain, but on the Supreme.

54
00:02:52.291 --> 00:02:54.500
Understand Krishna's message:

55
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.166
don't see sannyasa and yoga 
as separate from worldly life.

56
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:02.583
In both, a person moves from selfish feelings

57
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:06.166
toward selfless feelings.

58
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:09.833
Therefore, do your work, fulfill your duties,

59
00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:10.833
but

60
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:13.958
do it only as selfless service.

61
00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:21.500
This verse

62
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:27.958
contains the supreme definition of renunciation.

63
00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:32.083
Many people think renunciation means

64
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:35.416
that for spiritual progress

65
00:03:35.416 --> 00:03:39.458
they should separate from the world.

66
00:03:39.458 --> 00:03:43.708
Abandoning their worldly duties, they should

67
00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:47.541
go live somewhere far away in solitude.

68
00:03:47.541 --> 00:03:49.291
But

69
00:03:49.291 --> 00:03:52.875
true renunciation isn't

70
00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:55.208
abandoning action

71
00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:59.083
or moving away from the world.

72
00:03:59.083 --> 00:04:02.666
True renunciation is

73
00:04:02.666 --> 00:04:06.041
renouncing the desire for results.

74
00:04:06.041 --> 00:04:09.291
Where you remain in the world,

75
00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:12.625
while fulfilling your duties,

76
00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:16.666
you don't have attachment

77
00:04:16.666 --> 00:04:19.583
to the fruits of your actions.

78
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:21.625
Remember—

79
00:04:21.625 --> 00:04:26.708
your work, your family, your relationships—

80
00:04:26.708 --> 00:04:29.583
these are not obstacles

81
00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:32.666
to your spiritual progress.

82
00:04:32.666 --> 00:04:35.833
Rather, these are the opportunities

83
00:04:35.833 --> 00:04:40.083
I've given you to develop.

84
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:43.583
Every worldly duty of yours

85
00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:48.208
is an opportunity to practice renunciation, 
for spiritual upliftment, and

86
00:04:48.208 --> 00:04:52.958
to build a deeper connection with me.

87
00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:56.583
Just remember

88
00:04:56.583 --> 00:05:00.916
that all these duties must be done

89
00:05:00.916 --> 00:05:04.666
with a detached spirit.

90
00:05:04.666 --> 00:05:07.583
When you do any work 
without attachment to results,

91
00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:09.541
when you don't think during

92
00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:13.250
or after the work

93
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:19.000
whether you'll get success or failure,

94
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.958
then in every such moment 
you are practicing renunciation

95
00:05:22.958 --> 00:05:27.333
and spirituality.

96
00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:34.791
In family life,

97
00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:37.875
people often believe that

98
00:05:37.875 --> 00:05:41.333
spiritual progress and the 
path to becoming a yogi

99
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:46.500
and sannyasi is only for those

100
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.750
who abandon family

101
00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.750
or social bonds

102
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.458
and live in solitude.

103
00:05:54.458 --> 00:05:57.500
But this isn't true.

104
00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.791
You can live

105
00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:04.083
like a yogi

106
00:06:04.083 --> 00:06:05.625
and sannyasi

107
00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:08.500
even while fulfilling your family duties.

108
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.625
The secret lies in how

109
00:06:11.625 --> 00:06:19.083
you will fulfill your’s and 
your relationships desires.

110
00:06:19.083 --> 00:06:21.333
The secret isn't

111
00:06:21.333 --> 00:06:24.875
in abandoning duties or relationships.

112
00:06:24.875 --> 00:06:27.250
The secret is

113
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:30.541
in renouncing your attachment

114
00:06:30.541 --> 00:06:34.916
to that family duty or relationship.

115
00:06:34.916 --> 00:06:39.166
When you serve your family,

116
00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:40.416
it's natural

117
00:06:40.416 --> 00:06:45.250
to expect praise or gratitude.

118
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.791
The mind wants your effort to be appreciated.

119
00:06:49.791 --> 00:06:52.458
Right?

120
00:06:52.458 --> 00:06:54.375
But

121
00:06:54.375 --> 00:06:57.833
when this expectation isn't fulfilled,

122
00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:00.250
disappointment

123
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.666
and dissatisfaction arise,

124
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:07.500
which brings tension to your mind and often

125
00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:11.708
to family relationships as well.

126
00:07:11.708 --> 00:07:13.833
On the other hand, when

127
00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:17.250
you fulfill your family duties

128
00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.875
only with love and selfless spirit,

129
00:07:20.875 --> 00:07:24.583
without worrying about results,

130
00:07:24.583 --> 00:07:29.083
then you find peace and joy

131
00:07:29.083 --> 00:07:32.291
in that action or activity itself.

132
00:07:32.291 --> 00:07:36.666
This peace radiates from within you.

133
00:07:36.666 --> 00:07:40.416
By renouncing expectations and just

134
00:07:40.416 --> 00:07:42.916
immersing yourself in action,

135
00:07:42.916 --> 00:07:50.250
you can live the life of a 
true yogi even in your own home.

136
00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:57.333
In the professional environment,

137
00:07:57.333 --> 00:07:59.875
 there's a big misconception

138
00:07:59.875 --> 00:08:04.208
that spiritual progress and
 professional life are two

139
00:08:04.208 --> 00:08:07.750
completely different subjects.

140
00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.083
But

141
00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:12.250
you can live your professional life too

142
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.916
like a yogi and

143
00:08:13.916 --> 00:08:17.583
sannyasi.

144
00:08:17.583 --> 00:08:20.208
You just need to change

145
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:25.333
your perspective toward work.

146
00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:30.000
Often people work only
 when motivated by promotion,

147
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.250
honor,

148
00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:35.458
or financial gain.

149
00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:38.875
To an extent, this may be natural,

150
00:08:38.875 --> 00:08:42.958
but when these very desires

151
00:08:42.958 --> 00:08:47.208
become craving or attachment,

152
00:08:47.208 --> 00:08:50.791
then difficulty increases.

153
00:08:50.791 --> 00:08:55.916
When results aren't favorable, stress, worry,

154
00:08:55.916 --> 00:08:59.750
and disappointment grow.

155
00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:03.458
What should be done in this situation?

156
00:09:03.458 --> 00:09:06.750
Like a true yogi,

157
00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.916
do your work with complete dedication,

158
00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:15.458
but don't have attachment to 
the fruits of success,

159
00:09:15.458 --> 00:09:19.541
nor fear of failure.

160
00:09:19.541 --> 00:09:21.125
Because what's in your

161
00:09:21.125 --> 00:09:25.333
hands isn't the result, only the action.

162
00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:28.583
If success comes, be grateful

163
00:09:28.583 --> 00:09:31.500
because along with your effort,

164
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.541
other people

165
00:09:32.541 --> 00:09:35.833
and circumstances also contributed.

166
00:09:35.833 --> 00:09:39.208
If failure comes, analyze and

167
00:09:39.208 --> 00:09:42.416
bring changes to your work.

168
00:09:42.416 --> 00:09:44.666
A true yogi

169
00:09:44.666 --> 00:09:46.833
always remains steady

170
00:09:46.833 --> 00:09:50.291
and duty-bound.

171
00:09:50.291 --> 00:09:53.166
Which you too can become in your workplace.

172
00:09:53.166 --> 00:09:55.791
can become in your workplace.

173
00:09:55.791 --> 00:09:58.250
And by adopting this perspective,

174
00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:01.291
along with spiritual progress,

175
00:10:01.291 --> 00:10:03.833
you'll also gain peace

176
00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:06.625
and stability in your work.
